  "published": "2026-07-02T02:58:48.36Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.4.1 — Security/hardening (patch, but note the transport change below):\n      * ForAgent(url, secret) now REFUSES a plain-http URL to a non-loopback host and throws\n        ArgumentException. Point iSigner.AgentUrl at http://127.0.0.1:9090 (co-located agent) or use\n        https:// for a remote agent. A LAN http URL (e.g. http://192.168.x.x:9090) will now throw —\n        this is intentional (the ServiceAuth HMAC does not protect the document in transit over\n        cleartext). Loopback http is still allowed.\n      * Requires Newtonsoft.Json >= 13.0.3 (add a binding redirect on .NET Framework if an older\n        Newtonsoft is already present).\n      No wire-contract changes: works with signing-agent 1.4.x (incl. the 1.4.7 one-shot\n      prepare-session behaviour — CompletePdf sends Idempotency-Key=sessionId, so retries are safe).",
